From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:02:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wmiutils: Give WMI's status codes Windows' text, and their
 facilities their names.

Measured on Windows 11 build 29671 with tools/winmgmtsprobe (msgdump.c,
statustext.c):

- wmiutils' message table is the 189 messages of wbem\en-US's and
  wbem\zh-CN's wmiutils.dll.mui, success, WMI, provider and MOF ones;
  the Chinese texts are Windows'.
- GetErrorCodeText gives WMI's text for its codes and the system's for
  the others (a Win32 error's code's), with its line break, or with
  WBEMSTATUS_FORMAT_NO_NEWLINE a space; a code nothing has text for is
  WBEM_E_FAILED, any locale but the user's (0) an invalid parameter.
- GetFacilityCodeText names the facility: WMI for a code WMI has text
  for, Interface for another of FACILITY_ITF, <Null>, RPC, Dispatch,
  Storage, Win32, Windows, SSPI, Control, Cert, Internet, General.

The test checks the texts and facilities; on Windows it has no failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

